#{[{:activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088514 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088889 :tutorial/content "In mathematics, rectangular arrays containing numbers are called **matrices**. \n\nAs an example, consider the matrix $A$ below:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis particular matrix has $3$ rows and $3$ columns. The numbers in the matrix are called **entries** or **elements.**\n\nThe number of rows and columns in a matrix does not need to be the same. For example, consider another matrix that has $3$ rows and $4$ columns:\n\n$$\nM = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 13 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe **dimensions** of the matrix are the number of rows and the number of columns. For example, the matrix $M$ shown above has $3$ rows and $4$ columns. So, we write the dimensions of $M$ as $3 \\times 4$ (read as \"three by four\")." :tutorial/id #uuid "d68f01b8-8bc6-59a1-8d80-d284abbcdf6e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2968 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088515 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087693 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087500 :question/id #uuid "6587b5f1-8a44-556a-a95e-20c54dfebc04" :question/math-academy-id "e-4367" :question/problem "What are the dimensions of the matrix ${A},$ where \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix ${A}$ has $4$ rows and $3$ columns. Therefore, its dimensions are $4\\times 3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6ae25fc-16eb-598b-a288-742e4b46cb12" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050404}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476176} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2920f12-2ec4-5b28-9554-5e61dd2128da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218